                <pb facs="0373" n="285" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg285"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/2941: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Culbertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-03-10T12:00:00-04:00">March 10,
                        1933—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 12:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>44. My telegram No. 41.<anchor n="66" xml:id="d212-f1"/> Bolivian Minister told
                    Cruchaga yesterday under instructions from La Paz that his Government is not
                    disposed to modify in any way conditions laid down in its reply. Cruchaga said
                    that if this position was maintained in formal reply to the neutrals and to the
                    neighboring states he would be ready to cooperate in some drastic measures to
                    persuade Bolivia to accept arbitration presumably by embargoes.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
